This script takes the simulation data and then convert them to mimic real data to run through the eventcleaning

to just run the script locally on a single file 
./run_script.sh <YYYYMMDD> <SIMRUN> [GROPT|CARE]
./run_script.sh 20260803 muonkiet CARE
./run_script.sh 20260413 16190401_daro GROPT

./run_all this will run all on the local node (slow)

the 4th argument of SimRootFiles picks which simulation stage to read.
GROPT (the default) reads the ray traced photons out of T1 and makes the
1mm / 6mm camera views. CARE reads the FADC traces out of Events/T0 and
makes the 16x16 PE camera view from the sample at timebin 25. Both read the
same ISOG row for a shower, so the event label, the Sim tree and the Test
tree carry the same information either way. GROPT writes
datafiles_<date>_<simrun>.root as before, CARE writes
datafiles_<date>_<simrun>_CARE.root so the two do not overwrite.

to recompile 
./compile_script.sh

to submit as a job for all nights 
create the file that has all sim files to run over 
./get_folders_tocsv.sh 
then 
condor_submit convertsim2data.submit convertsim2data.submit
    uses ./run_condor.sh for inside the job















